#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/daemons.adoc:45
msgid ""
"image:daemons/logo.webp[width=128,height=117,float=\"right\"] The world is "
"awash with unseen magic that comes from the dark dimensions between time and "
"space.  It was introduced into the world when the great intra-spatial "
"gateways of the Old Ones collapsed, creating a rift in space and spewing "
"magically volatile warp-matter over the whole planet. Magic is a malleable "
"energy that can be harnessed and wielded, but the very act of doing so "
"reshapes and changes everyone and everything it comes into contact with. "
"Whether used for good or ill, magic is ultimately corrupting and dangerous."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/daemons.adoc:55
msgid ""
"The ancient gateways continue to leak raw magic from the dark dimension to "
"this day. The dark dimension is home to things of an altogether different "
"order to mortal creatures. These are not living creatures of flesh but a "
"network of ethereal forces whose consciousnesses continually flow and "
"interchange.  Individuality and linear thought are meaningless concepts in "
"the dark dimension. In that timeless, spaceless, nothingness there is only "
"endless being: a single moment extending through all eternity."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/daemons.adoc:67
msgid ""
"Just as magic pollutes and disfigures the material world so the dark "
"dimension is reshaped by the world of mortals. Thought, ambition, emotion "
"and other gross forms of individual consciousness leak from the material "
"universe. This focused consciousness overwhelms and transforms the naturally "
"guileless intelligence of the dark dimension. It becomes aware.  It "
"coalesces into a kind of distinct consciousness. Things stir in the dark "
"dimension. Gods, daemons and spirits are made manifest in the stuff of the "
"warp. Reshaped in turn by these newly created consciousnesses other lesser "
"beings are created, and so it goes on."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/daemons.adoc:83
msgid ""
"Thus are the gods of the Old World, and the bitterest agents of man’s own "
"destruction, self-created from the terror of mankind itself. There may be a "
"thousand gods or a million aspects of a single deity – it matters little. "
"The daemon armies of Chaos constantly reshape and reform in the face of "
"man’s ever shifting fears. Most of all men dread the elemental horrors of "
"life, and these are represented by the four great gods of the Marauder "
"tribes of the north. They are worshipped under many names and in many guises "
"but in the lands of the south they are recognised (by those who dare pursue "
"such studies) as the great powers of Khorne the Blood God, Tzeentch the "
"Changer of the Ways, Nurgle the Plague Lord, and Slaanesh the Lord of "
"Pleasure. These are the Great Gods of Chaos of which all other gods are but "
"parts or conjunctions. In the lands of the Empire many a theologist has been "
"burned for saying as much."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/daemons.adoc:87
#, no-wrap
msgid "Daemon army selector"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/daemons.adoc:92
#, no-wrap
msgid "include::partial$daemons.tsv[]\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/daemons.adoc:100
#, no-wrap
msgid "Ignore Terror"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/daemons.adoc:102
msgid ""
"All units ignore the −1 Attack penalty in combat for fighting terrifying "
"troops – you cannot frighten them at all."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/daemons.adoc:103
#, no-wrap
msgid "Daemonic Instability"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/daemons.adoc:110
msgid ""
"At the start of the player’s own Command phase, before making any "
"initiatives moves, all friendly Daemon units that have taken at least 1 "
"casualty (i.e. lost at least 1 stand out of 3) must make a ‘Daemonic "
"Instability’ test. Roll a D6. If the unit has lost 2 stands (i.e. has only 1 "
"stand remaining from 3)  and is further away than 20cm from a friendly "
"Daemon Wizard deduct 1 from the roll."
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/daemons.adoc:136
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"h|0–1\n"
"|One stand is destroyed – the daemons fade away and\n"
"are absorbed back into the Realm of Chaos from\n"
"which they came. Remove one stand from play. If\n"
"a character is with the unit and the last stand is\n"
"removed the character is destroyed too.\n"
"\n"
"h|2–3\n"
"|The unit becomes confused – if not already confused\n"
"the stand becomes confused as it is torn between this\n"
"world and the next.\n"
"\n"
"h|4–5\n"
"|No effect – unless the unit is confused in which case\n"
"it ceases to be confused as it is favoured with the\n"
"invigorating power of Chaos.\n"
"\n"
"h|6\n"
"|The unit regains one stand. The regained stand is\n"
"placed directly behind, in front or beside another\n"
"stand from the same unit, and facing the same\n"
"direction. If it is impossible to position the stand in\n"
"in this manner then the stand cannot be added.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/daemons.adoc:141
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[daemon-swarms,†1]]1. Daemon Swarms"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/daemons.adoc:143
msgid ""
"These cannot be driven back by shooting and do not roll for drive backs."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/daemons.adoc:146
msgid "A Daemon Swarm cannot be given a magic item."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/daemons.adoc:147
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[daemon-flyers,†2]]2. Daemon Flyers"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/daemons.adoc:148
msgid "These can fly."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/daemons.adoc:153
msgid ""
"Daemon flyers are an exception to the normal conventions for basing monsters "
"in that they face the long edge of the stand in the same way as infantry "
"rather than the short edge as most other monsters."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/daemons.adoc:154
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[greater-daemons,†3]]3. Greater Daemons"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/daemons.adoc:157
msgid ""
"Greater Daemons can fly regardless of whether the actual model has wings – "
"aerial propulsion is deemed feasible by sheer effort of will."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/daemons.adoc:159
msgid "Greater Daemons cause terror in their enemies."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/daemons.adoc:166
msgid ""
"A Greater Daemon that has accumulated 4–5 hits at the end of the Shooting or "
"Combat phase and is no longer engaged in combat is deemed to have been badly "
"hurt. Once a Greater Daemon is badly hurt accumulated hits are discounted "
"and its Hits and Attacks values are halved for the rest of the battle (to 3 "
"Hits and 4 Attacks)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/daemons.adoc:167
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[daemon-overlord,†4]]4. Daemon Overlord"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/daemons.adoc:174
msgid ""
"The Daemon Overlord is the army’s General and has the option of having the "
"powers of a Wizard for additional 25 points. If given magical powers the "
"Daemon Overlord can be given a magic item restricted to either a General or "
"a Wizard. Note that the Daemon Overlord is still a General and his command "
"range extends over the whole battlefield as for other Generals."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/daemons.adoc:175
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[daemonic-wings,†5]]5. Daemonic Wings"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/daemons.adoc:180
msgid ""
"Some of the creatures of the deep vaults of hell may have wings, some of "
"them fly on hovering discs and some even have the ability of disappearing "
"and reappearing wherever they want on the battlefield. Daemon characters may "
"be given the ability of flying."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/daemons.adoc:181
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[favour-of-the-gods,†6]]6. Favour of the Gods"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/daemons.adoc:185
msgid ""
"Demon Overlord, Lords or Sorcerers can be given the Favour of the Gods. The "
"character then gains +1 extra Attack and causes terror in its enemies as "
"described in the Warmaster rulebook."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/daemons.adoc:189
#, no-wrap
msgid "Daemonic spells"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/daemons.adoc:192
#, no-wrap
msgid "Summon Daemons"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/daemons.adoc:198
msgid ""
"_With a sulphurous blast of elemental power fresh Daemons emerge from the "
"warp to reinforce their beleaguered kindred._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/daemons.adoc:202
msgid ""
"This spell can be cast on any friendly Daemon unit of three stands that has "
"lost one or two stands as casualties. It does not matter whether the Wizard "
"can see the unit or not."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/daemons.adoc:210
msgid ""
"The unit regains one stand. The regained stand is placed directly behind, in "
"front or beside another stand from the same unit, and facing the same "
"direction. If the unit is already in combat the additional stand can be "
"placed so that it touches the enemy and will count as charging if the unit "
"charged. If it is impossible to position the stand in this manner, the spell "
"cannot be cast and will not work."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/daemons.adoc:212
#, no-wrap
msgid "Daemonic Rage"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/daemons.adoc:218
msgid ""
"_A keening cry of pure power rises upon daemonic lips as magical energy "
"surges through their eldritch bodies._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/daemons.adoc:220
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:199
msgid "This spell affects every friendly unit within range."
msgstr "Ce sort affecte toutes les unités amies à portée."

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/daemons.adoc:222
msgid "The spell lasts during the following Combat phase."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/daemons.adoc:226
msgid ""
"Every unit gains a bonus +1 attack. This attack can be allocated to any "
"stand in the unit and can be allocated to a different stand in each combat "
"round."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/daemons.adoc:228
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sorcerous Blast"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/daemons.adoc:235
msgid ""
"_With a single gesture a bolt of black lightning leaps from fingertip to the "
"foe, searing the enemy with a blast of dark power._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/daemons.adoc:239
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/lizardmen.adoc:250
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/skaven.adoc:269
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/tomb-kings.adoc:267
msgid ""
"This spell can be cast on an enemy unit. The Wizard must be able to see his "
"target to use this spell. The spell cannot be directed at a unit engaged in "
"combat."
msgstr ""
"Le Sorcier peut lancer ce sort sur une unité ennemie en vue. Il ne peut pas "
"être lancé sur une unité engagée en combat."

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/daemons.adoc:244
msgid ""
"The Sorcerous Blast is treated like three ordinary shooting attacks except "
"that armour has no effect (all targets count as having no armour). A unit "
"can be driven back by a Sorcerous Blast as with ordinary shooting."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/daemons.adoc:246
#, no-wrap
msgid "Frenzy of Chaos"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/daemons.adoc:252
msgid ""
"_Rumbling thunderous power surges through the daemonic ranks driving all "
"into a frenzied thirst for blood._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/daemons.adoc:256
msgid ""
"This spell can be cast upon a friendly unit which is engaged in combat and "
"that is within range. The Sorcerer does not have to be able to see the "
"target to cast the spell."
msgstr ""
"Ce sort peut être lancé sur une unité amie engagée au combat et à portée. Le "
"Sorcier n’est pas obligé de voir sa cible."

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/daemons.adoc:262
msgid ""
"The effect lasts until the end of the following Combat phase.  The unit can "
"re-roll any failed attacks in combat: take any dice that fail to score hits "
"and roll them again. Note that you cannot re-roll a dice that has already "
"been re-rolled either because of a spell, magic item or any other reason."
